Title: Night Shift

INT. WAREHOUSE - NIGHT

Rain hammers the tin roof. COLE (40s), a burly man with a shaved head and a scar across his chin, stacks CRATES. He wears a stained leather apron.

MARA (30s), wiry and quick, slips in through the side door holding a FLASHLIGHT.

MARA
You're late, Cole.

COLE
Traffic.

EXT. ALLEY - NIGHT

MARA sprints between the bins. The burly man lumbers after her, breathing hard.

MARA
(into her phone)
Cole's on me. He's huge, and he's got that scar.

COLE
Mara! Wait!

INT. WAREHOUSE - LATER

COLE, soaked, sits on a crate under a bare bulb. MARA hands him the FLASHLIGHT.

MARA
You look like you lost a fight with the weather.
